{"id":"caminho-da-fe","title":"Caminho da Fé","who":"Classic route · Brazil's pilgrimage to Aparecida, 34,000 pilgrims in 2025","when":"April to September (dry, cool)","vehicle":"On foot (or bike), about 12 days","kind":"walk","color":"#1e3a8a","summary":"Brazil's answer to the Camino de Santiago: 318 km on the main branch from Águas da Prata to the Basilica of Our Lady of Aparecida, through the coffee farms and mountains of southern Minas Gerais and the Serra da Mantiqueira. Pousadas for pilgrims, a credential to stamp, and steep climbs.","sources":[{"label":"Gazeta SP: Caminho da Fé, 318 km and the Serra da Mantiqueira","url":"https://www.gazetasp.com.br/turismo/caminho-da-fe-rota-de-318-km-ate-aparecida-exige-atencao-aos-desafios-da-serra-da-mantiqueira/"},{"label":"Associação dos Amigos do Caminho da Fé","url":"https://caminhodafe.com.br/ptbr/"}],"approximate":"Main towns of the classic branch; the path follows dirt roads and trails near the line shown.","km":347,"bbox":[-46.7893,-22.9364,-45.2346,-21.9466],"stops":[{"name":"Águas da Prata","place":"Águas da Prata, São Paulo","at":[-21.9464,-46.7192],"text":"A spa town and the start of the main branch, credential in hand.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/APrata_Centro.JPG/500px-APrata_Centro.JPG","page":"Águas da Prata","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:APrata_Centro.JPG","credit":"Fernando Medeiros","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Andradas","place":"Andradas, Minas Gerais","at":[-22.0693,-46.5708],"text":"Into Minas Gerais, wine and coffee country."},{"name":"Ouro Fino","place":"Ouro Fino, Minas Gerais","at":[-22.2826,-46.3695],"text":"Hill farms and the first long climbs."},{"name":"Borda da Mata","place":"Borda da Mata, Minas Gerais","at":[-22.2742,-46.1653],"text":"A town of pyjama makers on the pilgrims' road."},{"name":"Paraisópolis","place":"Paraisópolis, Minas Gerais","at":[-22.5542,-45.78],"text":"Towards the Mantiqueira."},{"name":"Luminosa","place":"Luminosa, Brazópolis","at":[-22.5926,-45.6133],"text":"The hardest days: up and over the Serra da Mantiqueira.","source":{"label":"Gazeta SP: the Mantiqueira","url":"https://www.gazetasp.com.br/turismo/caminho-da-fe-rota-de-318-km-ate-aparecida-exige-atencao-aos-desafios-da-serra-da-mantiqueira/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Montanhas_da_Serra_da_mantiqueira.jpg/500px-Montanhas_da_Serra_da_mantiqueira.jpg","page":"Mantiqueira Mountains","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montanhas_da_Serra_da_mantiqueira.jpg","credit":"Silvio serrano","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Campos do Jordão","place":"Campos do Jordão, São Paulo","at":[-22.7383,-45.5904],"text":"A mountain town at 1,600 m, cool and Alpine-looking.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Montagem_Campos_do_Jord%C3%A3o.jpg/500px-Montagem_Campos_do_Jord%C3%A3o.jpg","page":"Campos do Jordão","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montagem_Campos_do_Jord%C3%A3o.jpg","credit":"Allice Hunter","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Pindamonhangaba","place":"Pindamonhangaba, São Paulo","at":[-22.9364,-45.4623],"text":"Down into the Paraíba valley.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Pindamonhangaba_SP-Brazil_City_of_Aluminum_Recycling.JPG/500px-Pindamonhangaba_SP-Brazil_City_of_Aluminum_Recycling.JPG","page":"Pindamonhangaba","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pindamonhangaba_SP-Brazil_City_of_Aluminum_Recycling.JPG","credit":"Onethatlovespeace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Aparecida","place":"Basílica de Aparecida","at":[-22.8509,-45.2338],"text":"The huge basilica of Brazil's patron saint, the end of the way.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Basilica_of_the_National_Shrine_of_Our_Lady_of_Aparecida%2C_2007.jpg/500px-Basilica_of_the_National_Shrine_of_Our_Lady_of_Aparecida%2C_2007.jpg","page":"Basil